# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/).

***

## [0.3.0] - 2026-06-06

### Added
- `src/sql_agent/` — new core library package (replaces scattered duplicates):
  - `config.py` — `Settings` dataclass; no import side-effects; `from_env()` factory; backwards-compat helpers re-exported
  - `db.py` — `get_engine()` (LRU-cached per URI) and `execute_sql()` shared by all entry-points
  - `llm.py` — `call_ollama()` with exponential back-off retry (replaces duplicated `requests.post` blocks)
  - `validator.py` — `clean_sql()`, `validate_sql()`, `ensure_top()` (single source of truth)
  - `prompts.py` — canonical `SYSTEM_PROMPTS` dict (`simple` / `prompt` / `full`)
- `tests/test_validator.py` — 27 unit tests for `clean_sql`, `validate_sql`, `ensure_top`
- `tests/test_config.py` — unit tests for `Settings` validation and URI building
- `pyproject.toml` — proper package definition with `[project.scripts]` console entry-points
- `python-dotenv` added as dependency (falls back to manual parser if not installed)
- `SQLITE_DB_PATH` env var added to `.env.example`

### Changed
- `agents/main.py`, `agents/langchain_sql.py`, `agents/nlq_with_sqlite.py` — all now import from `sql_agent.*`; no more `sys.path` hacks
- `runners/nlq.py`, `runners/langsql.py` — duplicate `_call_ollama`, `_validate_env`, `_get_engine` replaced by `sql_agent.*` imports
- `requirements.txt` — all packages now have minimum version pins
- `config.py` (root) — converted to backwards-compat shim; real logic in `src/sql_agent/config.py`
- `README.md` — updated project structure, new usage examples, test instructions, updated How It Works diagram

### Fixed
- `config.py` used to call `load_env_file()` as a module-level side-effect on every import — now opt-in via `Settings.from_env()` or explicit `load_env_file()`
- `agents/main.py` used `sys.path.insert` hack to reach root `config.py` — removed

***

## [0.2.0] - 2026-06-06

### Added
- `langchain-sql.py` — advanced SQL Server NLQ agent with full SQL validation pipeline:
  - `extract_sql()`: multi-strategy SQL extractor (fenced block, first-SELECT, fallback)
  - `normalize_table_references()`: auto-corrects 2-part refs to 3-part `[DB].[Schema].[Table]`
  - `validate_sql()`: blocks dangerous keywords, enforces SELECT-only, checks allowed tables
  - Configurable `ALLOWED_TABLES` list for access control
  - Global connection cache for LLM, engine, and database objects
- `langsql.py` — Auction DB NLQ engine using raw Ollama HTTP API (no LangChain agent):
  - `repair_sql()`: auto-fixes LIMIT→TOP and DISTINCT/TOP ordering
  - Interactive REPL loop with retry logic (3 attempts on Ollama timeout)
  - Returns results as pandas DataFrame with lock timeout set
- `nlq_with_sqlite.py` — SQLite backend variant for local testing without SQL Server
- `prompt_based_nlq.py` — prompt-driven SQL Server agent using `config.py` credentials
- `simple_nlq.py` — minimal single-question SQL Server agent for quick smoke tests
- `create_db.py` — script to generate a sample SQLite database (customers + orders tables)
- `sample.db` — prebuilt SQLite sample database for immediate local testing

### Changed
- `config.py`: improved docstrings; `OLLAMA_BASE_URL` now documented as optional with default `http://localhost:11434`; `get_ollama_config()` usage example updated

***

## [0.1.0] - 2026-04-10

### Added
- `main.py` — CLI entry point using `--prompt` argument to query the database in natural language
- `config.py` — secure configuration module that loads all credentials from `.env`
- `.env.example` — environment variable template for Ollama and SQL Server settings
- `requirements.txt` — project dependencies
- `.gitignore` — excludes `.env` and generated files from version control
- `README.md` — setup, usage, configuration, and troubleshooting guide

### Architecture
- Gemma 3 (via Ollama) as the local LLM backend — no API key required
- LangChain `create_sql_agent` with `ZERO_SHOT_REACT_DESCRIPTION` agent type
- SQL Server connectivity via `mssql+pyodbc` and SQLAlchemy
- Support for both SQL Server Authentication and Windows Authentication
- All credentials isolated in `.env` — zero hardcoded values in source code
